# agent.env — the ONLY place a coding harness is named.
# loop.sh and supervisor.sh source this file. Switching harnesses is a
# one-line edit here; no contract file (AUTOPILOT/ROADMAP/STATE) ever
# names a harness.
#
# The builder contract any harness must satisfy:
#   - reads files in the project dir
#   - runs shell commands (build/test/path_test.sh)
#   - can be invoked non-interactively with a prompt
#   - exits when the iteration is done
#
# Reviewer rule: REVIEWER_CMD should be a DIFFERENT harness than
# BUILDER_CMD (cross-model review finds what same-model review inherits).
# If only one harness is available, fall back to same-harness review in a
# clean worktree with fresh context — weaker, but better than skipping.

ITERATION_PROMPT='You are the Chorus autonomous builder. Read docs/AUTONOMOUS_BUILD.md (the mission brief), then STATE.md, ROADMAP.md (current goal), AUTOPILOT.md, and the last 3 BUILD_LOG.md entries. Execute ONE iteration per that brief and the AUTOPILOT procedure, then exit.'

# --- Default: Claude Code builds, Codex reviews ---
BUILDER_CMD='claude -p "$ITERATION_PROMPT" --permission-mode acceptEdits'
REVIEWER_CMD='codex exec'

# --- Alternate: Codex builds, Claude Code reviews ---
# BUILDER_CMD='codex exec "$ITERATION_PROMPT"'
# REVIEWER_CMD='claude -p'

# --- Notes per harness ---
# Claude Code: `claude -p` is headless mode. Tune permissions to match
#   AUTOPILOT's allowed-list (acceptEdits covers file edits; shell commands
#   prompt unless allowed via settings). A project .claude/settings.json
#   can pre-approve the build/test/lint commands so iterations don't stall.
# Codex CLI: `codex exec` is the non-interactive mode; set approval policy
#   to match the same allowed-list.
# Anything else: satisfies the four-line contract above? It works.

# --- Budget ---
# BUDGET_MODE=api    -> dollar caps are the binding constraint (metered API)
# BUDGET_MODE=plan   -> subscription usage windows are the real budget;
#                       dollar caps are mostly inert. (Claude Max, ChatGPT Plus)
BUDGET_MODE=plan
SESSION_CAP_USD=25
DAILY_CAP_USD=75
WATCHDOG_N=3

# --- Usage limits (the third terminal state: paused) ---
# Patterns marking a builder failure as a LIMIT (pause + retry), not a
# crash. Case-insensitive extended regex matched against builder output.
LIMIT_PATTERNS='usage limit|rate limit|429|too many requests|try again (later|in)|quota|capacity|overloaded|limit (reached|exceeded)'

# Probe-and-backoff: sleep, retry once, still limited -> sleep again.
# Neutral by design — no harness window math to parse or maintain.
LIMIT_SLEEP_S=1800          # 30 min between probes
LIMIT_MAX_WAIT_S=21600      # stop pausing after 6h; write [blocked]

# Optional failover: second harness takes over while the primary is
# limited. OFF by default — mid-run model switching puts two models'
# opinions in one codebase between reviews. Enable when daytime idle
# hours are expensive; cross-model review still applies at the next
# goal boundary.
# FALLBACK_BUILDER_CMD='codex exec "$ITERATION_PROMPT"'
FALLBACK_BUILDER_CMD=''

